KG42.register("rules-146af7deb1315df20c395162",{"id":"15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R004","paper":"15-multiagent_reverse_auction","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R004","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market clearing","process_stage":"clearing","market_meaning":"The local allocation process uses the qualified bidder's submitted supply to check whether that bidder can cover all demand. Scope: Hour-ahead allocation of the grid-connected microgrid's lumped demand among qualified DER bidders. The aggregator coordinates local procurement by buying the qualified amount of power from DERs, with the remaining demand purchased from the utility. Scope: Local DER procurement in the grid-connected microgrid's hour-ahead reverse auction under insufficient supply. Condition: Total supply is less than demand and some bidders participate in the auction. Local procurement aims to purchase the required amount of power at the lowest cost. Scope: Procurement objective for the microgrid's lumped load in the hour-ahead reverse auction. The first qualified bidder is supposed to cover the majority of the total demand. Scope: Demand allocation among qualified bidders in the hour-ahead reverse auction. The second qualifying bidder covers the remaining demand. Scope: Residual demand allocation among qualified bidders in the hour-ahead reverse auction. Condition: A supply deficit remains after the first qualified bidder's contribution.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function clearing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.supply","clearing.local","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"bidding.supply","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E19"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E002","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E21"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Demand allocation among qualified bidders in the hour-ahead reverse auction. | Hour-ahead allocation of the grid-connected microgrid's lumped demand among qualified DER bidders. | Local DER procurement in the grid-connected microgrid's hour-ahead reverse auction under insufficient supply. | Procurement objective for the microgrid's lumped load in the hour-ahead reverse auction. | Residual demand allocation among qualified bidders in the hour-ahead reverse auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E21"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local allocation process uses the qualified bidder's submitted supply to check whether that bidder can cover all demand. Scope: Hour-ahead allocation of the grid-connected microgrid's lumped demand among qualified DER bidders.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E19"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The aggregator coordinates local procurement by buying the qualified amount of power from DERs, with the remaining demand purchased from the utility. Scope: Local DER procurement in the grid-connected microgrid's hour-ahead reverse auction under insufficient supply. Condition: Total supply is less than demand and some bidders participate in the auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E21"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Local procurement aims to purchase the required amount of power at the lowest cost. Scope: Procurement objective for the microgrid's lumped load in the hour-ahead reverse auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The first qualified bidder is supposed to cover the majority of the total demand. Scope: Demand allocation among qualified bidders in the hour-ahead reverse auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The second qualifying bidder covers the remaining demand. Scope: Residual demand allocation among qualified bidders in the hour-ahead reverse auction. Condition: A supply deficit remains after the first qualified bidder's contribution.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E15","location":{"location_id":"src-1b3df4bc99-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Proposed Methodology","anchor_text":"The aggregator manages the communication and the infor- his mation exchange between participants to ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The aggregator manages the communication and the information exchange between participants to minimize the cost of the electricity to be purchased for the lumped load. The aggregator agent is the main entity operating the auction process. Its task is to solicit bids form the agents registered to the yellow pages, and to invite them to participate in the auction. The ultimate goal is to purchase the required amount of power with the lowest cost. DERs submit bids to the DER aggregator, declaring the power available to sell and the price for the next hour. Each DER has a generation capacity, marginal cost, and availability."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E19","location":{"location_id":"src-1b3df4bc99-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Proposed Methodology","anchor_text":"to check whether qualiﬁed bidder’s submission is able to cover all demand. The ﬁrst qualiﬁed bidder ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"One more process is defined to check whether qualified bidder’s submission is able to cover all demand. The first qualified bidder is supposed to cover the majority of the total demand. However, if there is still deficit of supply, the second qualifying bidder covers the remaining amount."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E21","location":{"location_id":"src-1b3df4bc99-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Proposed Methodology","anchor_text":"to check whether qualiﬁed bidder’s submission is able to cover all demand. The ﬁrst qualiﬁed bidder ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"If all base prices of the generation units in the microgrid are higher than the utility base price and none of them are interested in participating in the auction, the aggregator agent buys all required power from the utility. If the total supply is less than the demand and some of the bidders are participating in the auction, the aggregator agent buys qualified amount of power from the DERs and the remaining is purchased from the utility."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No source-defined variable symbol or domain is available for this rule's clearing quantities. The supplied evidence describes 'qualified bidder's submission', 'all demand', 'majority', 'remaining amount' and 'qualified amount' in natural language and algorithmic branches only; adding typed variables would invent notation and domains.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed parameter symbol or value is defined in this rule's evidence. Numeric prices and example kW values elsewhere in the paper are outside R004's clearing constraints and are not imported without source-scoped definitions."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-activation","v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-validation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E19","quote":"One more process is defined to check whether qualified bidder’s submission is able to cover all demand."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E15","quote":"DERs submit bids to the DER aggregator, declaring the power available to sell and the price for the next hour."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E21","quote":"If the total supply is less than the demand and some of the bidders are participating in the auction, the aggregator agent buys qualified amount of power from the DERs and the remaining is purchased from the utility."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E15","quote":"The ultimate goal is to purchase the required amount of power with the lowest cost."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E19","quote":"The first qualified bidder is supposed to cover the majority of the total demand."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E19","quote":"However, if there is still deficit of supply, the second qualifying bidder covers the remaining amount."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"6093629bf511ce999870ad1e38202397162d4a48af6707d11ead1a7a98921365","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"The rule is a clearing/allocation process, but the supplied unreviewed evidence gives only qualitative coverage checks and allocation branches. It defines no equation, variable or parameter symbols, units, domains, or optimization form; terms such as 'majority' and 'qualified amount' remain undefined. The existing C001-C005 constraints are therefore retained as procedural and not formalized, and no x/theta objects are added without source-defined notation. B re-extraction is needed before any mathematical expression can be supported.","bindings":[],"revision_requests":["B re-extraction: obtain source-defined symbols, units, and domains for the quantities used by v141-b-g01-E14, v141-b-g01-E19, and v141-b-g01-E21, specifically total demand, a qualified bidder's submitted supply, power reference/allocation to first and second qualified bidders, 'qualified amount', and 'majority'. If the source gives no such mathematical definitions, record the clearing branches as procedural rather than inferring them.","C.1 revision: if B supplies those definitions, add the corresponding typed x/theta objects and any necessary allocation edges to the frozen graph; otherwise retain the current V/E and keep C001-C005 as non-formalized procedural constraints."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
